      "math_academy_id": "e-1506",
      "problem": "What is the recursive formula for the following geometric sequence?\n\n$$\n1, \\: 4, \\: 16, \\: \\ldots\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The recursive formula for a geometric sequence with common ratio $r$ takes the form\n\n$$\na_{n+1} = r \\cdot a_{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the first term is $a_1={\\color{blue}1},$ and we can calculate the common ratio $r$ as\n\n$$\nr = \\dfrac{a_2}{a_1} = \\dfrac 4 1 = {\\color{red}4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the recursive formula is\n\n$$\na_{n+1} = {\\color{red}4} \\cdot a_{n} , \\qquad a_1 = {\\color{blue}1}, \\qquad n\\geq 1.\n$$",
